      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Core Practices (Demonstrates H1 -> H2 -> H3 hierarchy) -->
    <section id="practices">
      <h2>Core Daily Practices</h2>
      <p>Building sustainable habits takes time. Here are three key areas to focus on first:</p>

      <article>
        <h3>1. Composting &amp; Soil Health</h3>
        <p>Organic kitchen scraps make up a large portion of household waste. Diverting them to compost returns vital nutrients to the soil and reduces methane emissions in landfills.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>2. Energy Conservation</h3>
        <p>Switching to LED lighting, sealing windows, and utilizing natural sunlight can drastically cut household energy demands.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>3. Rainwater Harvesting</h3>
        <p>Collecting rain in barrels or rain gardens reduces strain on municipal water systems and keeps landscape plants thriving during dry spells.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: Getting Started List -->
    <section id="resources">
      <h2>First Steps for Beginners</h2>
      <p>Follow this checklist to start your journey today:</p>
      
      <ol>
        <li>Audit your weekly household trash to identify single-use plastics.</li>
        <li>Set up a small countertop compost bin for fruit and vegetable scraps.</li>
        <li>Replace high-frequency incandescent bulbs with LEDs.</li>
        <li>Start a small herb container garden on a sunlit windowsill.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

